answer.worked:
Using $(0,0)$ and $(5,60)$:
$$\begin{align*}
\text{Rate of flow} &= \frac{\text{rise}}{\text{run}}\\
&= \frac{60-0}{5-0}\\
&= 12\text{ L/min}
\end{align*}$$

$1\text{ hour}=60\text{ minutes}$.
$$\begin{align*}
V &= 12t\\
V &= 12(60)\\
V &= 720\text{ L}
\end{align*}$$

$$\begin{align*}
1800 &= 12t\\
\frac{1800}{12} &= t\\
t &= 150\text{ min}
\end{align*}$$

